anya (docs): I'm opening a concise PR consolidating quota + rate docs, with practical SDK snippets and dashboard permalinks. Draft link: https://git.internal/redwood/docs/pull/2517 :wave:

sam (eng-platform): Nice. Two quick clarifications: 1) which unit aggregation do you show as primary (hourly vs per-minute)? 2) are the examples using the rotated header name?

anya (docs): Primary is hourly for public docs, per-minute kept in an ops subsection. All examples use X-RW-Usage; added a cross-reference note mapping the legacy X-Usage-Tokens header to the new one for older SDKs.

lia (devex): Please include a tiny JS snippet demonstrating parsing the response series for both group_by=1h and group_by=1m. People often mix up ordering of points. Sample I suggest is included in the PR.

anya (docs): Yep, added this snippet under "SDK snippets":
```
// hourly aggregation
const res = await fetch('/v1/usage?from=-1h&group_by=1h', {
  headers: { Authorization: `Bearer ${process.env.RW_KEY}`, 'X-RW-Usage': 'project=acme,env=prod' }
});
const body = await res.json();
console.log(body.series[0].points.map(p => p.value));
```

sam (eng-platform): Good. Add Grafana panel permalink (panel id 42) and an explicit troubleshooting line about double-counting when teams forget to change routing headers during canary -> stable flips.

anya (docs): Added permalink to panel 42 and this troubleshooting note: "If totals appear doubled after a rollout, verify routing headers and ensure canary/stable use distinct meter_key values."

mike (product): Also add a succinct callout about burst credits: "Dashboard 'available' reflects committed tier + temporary burst; billing reconciles against daily meter windows (UTC)." Keep it short.

lia (devex): One more: include a short paragraph explaining that fallback routing can affect per-model meter attribution and that per-route snapshots help reconcile discrepancies.

anya (docs): Included. I also added a follow-up issue link to add a small test prompt set that triggers high token churn so Optimize can produce batching suggestions. Not blocking this PR.

